Objective: Distribute electricity to balance supply and demand, reduce peak load and keep the grid reliable.
Why RL is suitable: Distribution decisions are time-coupled through storage and demand, and conditions are uncertain, so a learned adaptive policy outperforms fixed schedules.
Agent and environment: The agent is the grid distribution controller; the environment is the grid with its generators, storage, consumers and time-varying demand.
State space: Current demand, available generation and renewable supply, storage level, time of day, and electricity price.
Action space: Route power to regions, charge or discharge storage, defer flexible load, or shed non-critical load.
